From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:44:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] UefiPayloadPkg: Add a slot for a bootloader-supplied NIC
 driver

The network stack gets NIC drivers only from the prebuilt Realtek and
ASIX binaries, so a bootloader build for a platform with another NIC
can't add its own UNDI or SNP driver.

When NETWORK_UNDI_DRIVER is defined, put
UefiPayloadPkg/NetworkDrivers/UndiDxe.efi, supplied by the bootloader
build, into the FV as a driver. A driver that produces only NII needs
NETWORK_SNP_ENABLE as well.

The driver's dependency expression requires gNetworkBootPolicyGuid,
which NetworkBootPolicyDxe installs unless the bootloader's CFR option
"network_stack" is 0, taking the stored value or else the CFR default.
Then no NIC driver runs and the firmware has no network boot, while
the OS still sees the NIC. Without the option the driver always runs.

The expression also requires gEfiSimpleTextOutProtocolGuid, which
ConSplitterDxe installs when it sets gST->ConOut. Some drivers check
gST->ConOut at entry: iPXE's returns EFI_NOT_AVAILABLE_YET without it.

